# Reference brain 4 of 4: the best a hand-built brain gets, with no network in it.
#
# Everything the vocabulary offers except a Dense Layer. Against the racer it is
# about a sixth quicker over a lap and takes the same nothing in damage.
#
# What it does that the racer does not:
#
#   * Brakes for the corner after next as well as the next one, so it is already
#     slowing when it arrives rather than slowing because it arrived.
#   * Works out a corner speed instead of holding a fixed one: the sharper the
#     turn ahead, the lower the speed it will allow, and the more damaged the car
#     the lower again. A hurt car stops driving like a healthy one.
#   * Steers on two spreads of rays at once. The narrow pair shapes the line
#     through a corner; the wide pair is what saves it when the line is wrong.
#   * Filters its own steering through memory. The wheel holds where it is and
#     moves a share of the way to where it wants to be each tick, which is a
#     first-order filter and a legal loop — it passes through an accumulator.
#   * Latches DRS rather than switching it. It opens on a long straight and drops
#     the moment the road shortens or the route bends, and because reset beats set
#     inside an accumulator the closing condition always wins. Without the latch
#     the wing chatters open and shut at the threshold.
#   * Watches the car ahead on radar and pulls gently to the side it is not on.
#
# The numbers below were found by sweeping them against four tracks, three of
# which it had never seen. They are a local best, not a proof.
#
# One of them was found somewhere else. Sweeping on empty tracks produced a brain
# that was quickest on its own and the most damaged of any of them in a pack --
# it was tuned solo, so it had been tuned for solo. Halving push_k, the lane
# change it makes around a car ahead, cut its damage in a fourteen-car race from
# 40% to 26%, got it further round in the same time, and cost nothing over a
# flying lap. It had been steering into traffic rather than past it.

format 1
name "Ace"

tray tray_1 "DRS"
    at 1743.93359375 1723.8760986328125
    size 2117.89501953125 601.00244140625
    colour 7

tray tray_2 "Steering"
    at 1469.88720703125 644.96929931640625
    size 3655.06005859375 941.823486328125
    colour 4

tray tray_3 "Brake+Throtle"
    at 1659.2508544921875 -161.33815002441406
    size 2680.55615234375 734.595947265625
    colour 2

tray tray_4 "Straight Detect"
    at -134.95343017578125 83.04864501953125
    size 1187.3756103515625 496.6083984375
    colour 1

tray tray_5 "Damage Detect"
    at -11.14263916015625 -267.34255981445312
    size 912.0360107421875 326.310546875

